  "narrative": {
    "northStar": "The Herbarium Sheet",
    "overview": "**Creative North Star: \"The Herbarium Sheet\"**\n\nYour practice is a living specimen mounted on a sheet. Every screen is a cool white mount laid on a sage ground, and the one thing that grows on it is a linden drawn from your sessions: a sprout at first, a tree with roots and blossom after months. The plant is the progress display; numbers stay few and large, and nothing else competes with it.\n\nThe world is quiet and botanical rather than wellness-soft. Hierarchy comes from weight and size in a single sans (Golos Text), not from colour or ornament. Sheets are plain rounded rectangles with no borders and no shadows; depth is the step from ground to sheet. Specimen green marks growth and the one primary action on a screen; ochre is reserved for the soil line and earned marks. Dark mode is the same sheet at night: green-black mount, pale leaf ink.\n\nIt deliberately leaves behind the earlier cream ground, serif headlines and terracotta card stack.",
    "keyCharacteristics": [
      "Cool mount ground, flat sheets, no borders or shadows on content.",
      "One sans family carries everything; a large numeral is the only display moment on Home.",
      "The linden tree, drawn at one shared scale for every stage, is the signature.",
      "Green means growth or \"go\"; ochre means soil or earned.",
      "Light and dark are designed as a pair, not inverted."
    ],
    "rules": [
      {
        "name": "The One Green Rule",
        "body": "Each screen has at most one filled green button. Secondary actions are ghost buttons on `mount-ground-2`.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Ochre Is Earth Rule",
        "body": "Ochre appears only as soil, blossom and earned marks. If it isn't ground or reward, it isn't ochre.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Weight Not Colour Rule",
        "body": "Hierarchy is carried by size and weight. Don't colour a heading to make it louder.",
        "section": "typography"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Cyrillic Parity Rule",
        "body": "Every face used must render Cyrillic. Fraunces does not, so it never leaves the wordmark.",
        "section": "typography"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Flat Sheet Rule",
        "body": "A sheet never gets a shadow or an outline. If two things need separating, put them on separate sheets.",
        "section": "elevation"
      }
    ],
    "dos": [
      "**Do** take every colour from `useColors()` and design light and night together.",
      "**Do** keep one filled green button per screen; everything else is ghost or an icon step.",
      "**Do** let the tree be the progress display: one shared scale across stages, drawn on the ochre soil line.",
      "**Do** keep text in Golos Text through `Txt` so EN, UK and RU match.",
      "**Do** keep controls at 48px tall (buttons) or give smaller round controls hit slop."
    ],
    "donts": [
